# Database and security

- Never edit an already-applied Supabase migration. Prefer updating an unapplied migration in place only when it has never been applied anywhere; otherwise add a new forward-only corrective migration. Before changing an existing migration file, compare its version with the remote migration list.
- Local `supabase db reset` success does not prove the production upgrade path. When fixing applied-migration drift, add an upgrade-path test that reproduces the drifted catalog, applies the new migration, and asserts `pg_catalog` state.
- Production preflight must compare expected functions/triggers/policies with `pg_catalog`, not migration history alone.
- Do not apply migrations to remote Supabase unless explicitly asked.
- Prefer SECURITY DEFINER helpers with `SET search_path = public` for membership checks to avoid RLS recursion.
- SECURITY DEFINER functions default to PUBLIC EXECUTE — explicitly revoke PUBLIC (and authenticated, for trigger/maintenance helpers) unless a read-only helper is required by RLS.
- Pick identity fields (`id`, `user_id`, `week_id` / `playoff_round_id`, `submitted_at`) are immutable for all authenticated users, including commissioners. Check immutability before commissioner exceptions. Commissioner authority uses `OLD` week/round ids.
- Players may change only `team_id` on their own picks before kickoff/lock; insert/update timestamps and pick provenance (`game_id`, `result_source`, `result_override_reason`) are database-controlled.
- Treat `locks_at <= now()` and `scheduled_kickoff_at <= now()` as locked (exact timestamp is locked).
- Keep regular-season and playoff used-team lists separate; serialize reuse checks with namespaced advisory locks.
- `teams` is migration-managed reference data; authenticated app users are read-only.
- Never claim RLS is verified from reading SQL alone — run the database authorization tests when local Supabase is available.
- Do not weaken application-table RLS to make tests pass; grant only the `tests` schema helpers to authenticated.
